// The walk cycle of a figure (WP11.6i, crates/sf_render/src/walk.rs). Render only: nothing here
// reaches the simulation. Applied only to figure models whose six nodes have their origins at the
// joints (the glb loader checks it; the set v3 figures do not, and keep gliding).
//
// The phase of the cycle follows the distance a unit travels, one cycle per `stride_m` (two
// steps), so the feet do not slide and a slower unit steps slower; `stride_m` belongs with
// `leg_swing_deg`: 4 * hip * sin(swing) = 4 * 0.9 * sin(30°) = 1.80 m for the trial figure.
// Wall time only blends between standing and walking (`blend_s`).
//
// Cadence (fix round 1): the rifleman moves 0.7 cells/s = 2.8 m/s, a jog. With 24° and 1.46 m it
// took 3.8 steps/s and scurried; 30° and 1.80 m give 1.56 cycles/s = 3.1 steps/s, a jogging
// cadence, at the cost of a deeper bob (0.9 * (1 - cos 30°) = 0.12 m). Drawn larger (far zoom) the
// stride grows with the model, so the cadence drops with the drawn scale.
//
// `max_step_m`: a unit that moves more than this between two frames (2 m at true size) keeps its
// phase. At 2.8 m/s that needs under 1.4 frames per second of game time, e.g. 4x fast-forward
// below about 6 fps; the figure then stops stepping for those frames.
(
    leg_swing_deg: 30.0,       // each leg either way of upright, about the hip
    arm_swing_deg: 24.0,       // the free arm, opposite to the leg on its side
    rifle_arm_swing_deg: 5.0,  // the arm that carries the rifle swings little
    lean_deg: 4.0,             // forward lean of torso and head at full walk
    stride_m: 1.80,            // metres per cycle at true model size
    blend_s: 0.25,             // seconds from standing to walking and back
    max_step_m: 2.0,           // a longer jump per frame does not advance the phase
)
